  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "First: it attempts to place the nodes at the cursor. The way it does that is by picking one specific node and puts that at the cursor, then all the other nodes will be arranged around that as if they are children of it. The problem is that the node it picks is completely unpredictable. It's not random, but it appears to be the first according to some index. Because of the unpredictability, you have no idea where your nodes are going to go.\n\nSecond: once you have pasted a bunch of nodes, they are by default not selected.\n\nThese two issues combined means that it is very common to duplicate a group of nodes and they end up mashed together with a different group, so your only option is to undo and paste it somewhere else.",
